#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 255 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Outputs cursor movement \, mouse wheel events and mouse
button presses as control messages. Polling can be turned on and off
from the inlet. The polling interval is set globally via the polltime
method.;
#X text 240 153 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 178 • Interactive patches driven by the mouse — using cursor
position and mouse button presses to control sound parameters \, trigger
events or navigate a patch without a dedicated GUI element.;
#X text 250 248 • Gesture and motion control — mapping cursor motion
or mouse wheel scrolling to sound parameters \, for example in performance
or installation setups where the mouse or trackpad acts as a continuous
controller.;
